* Functional study model: dual-rail supervisor for the SubBass series mute.
* Not a physical IC or a manufacturing-ready protection circuit.
* VP/VN are the signed analog rails relative to GND.
* CTRL high = audio passes through the external normally-open switch S1.
* Both rails must exceed 13 V magnitude to qualify; either below 12 V resets.
* 200 ms nominal qualification after rails become valid; ~1 us reset time constant.
* RAIL_OK and TIMER are observable diagnostic outputs in volts.
.SUBCKT SUBBASS_MUTE_CTRL VP VN GND CTRL RAIL_OK TIMER
BREF REF GND V={max(0,min(5,V(VP,GND)))}
BSENSE SENSE GND V={min(V(VP,GND),-V(VN,GND))}
SVALID REF RAIL_OK SENSE GND RAIL_VALID OFF
RVALID RAIL_OK GND 10k
BBAD BAD GND V={V(RAIL_OK,GND)>2.5 ? 0 : 5}
BCHARGE CHARGE GND V={V(RAIL_OK,GND)>2.5 ? 5 : 0}
RDELAY CHARGE TIMER 200k
CDELAY TIMER GND 1u
SRESET TIMER GND BAD GND TIMER_RESET
BCTRL CTRL GND V={(V(RAIL_OK,GND)>2.5 && V(TIMER,GND)>3.160602794) ? V(REF,GND) : 0}
.MODEL RAIL_VALID SW(VT=12.5 VH=0.5 RON=1 ROFF=1e12)
.MODEL TIMER_RESET SW(VT=2.5 VH=0 RON=1 ROFF=1e12)
.ENDS SUBBASS_MUTE_CTRL

* Ideal SERIES audio mute, equivalent to RON=1 ohm / ROFF=1 Gohm.
* Behavioral conductance gives consistent DC, TRAN and small-signal AC results.
* The native SW in this installed ngspice build stayed open during AC even
* with a DC 5 V control; do not use that AC result as filter attenuation.
* CTRL high = PASS. No physical charge injection, bounce or turn-off delay.
.SUBCKT SUBBASS_MUTE_SWITCH IN OUT CTRL GND
BPATH IN OUT I={V(IN,OUT)*(V(CTRL,GND)>2.5 ? 1 : 1e-9)}
.ENDS SUBBASS_MUTE_SWITCH
